From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vladimir Levin <vmpstr@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:28:38 -0700
Subject: VT: Don't paint view transition content under SVG reference filters

VTs can have pixels of cross-origin frames, file:// frames and plugins.
SVG reference filters must not be applied to such content (see the
PreventSvgFilterPaint deprecation and crbug.com/476646486), but that
mitigation only covers the remote frame and plugin foreign layers, and
in-process cross-origin frames. A reference filter on the view
transition pseudo-elements, or on an ancestor of a subframe or scope
with a view transition, was therefore still applied to
DisplayItem::kForeignLayerViewTransitionContent.

This patch records all three kForeignLayerViewTransitionContent foreign
layers under the parent of the highest effect with a reference filter,

Note that whether the content actually contains such pixels isn't
tracked (e.g. the old snapshot of a cross-document transition is
captured by the previous document). There's a TODO for that.

A new ViewTransitionPreventSvgFilterPaint deprecation (and use counter)
is reported when a filter is removed

Bug: 568974861
Change-Id: Ic188e4e24f5743d5183fb2dfcebc14e284b7a929
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8521561
Reviewed-by: Philip Rogers <pdr@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Ari Chivukula <arichiv@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Vladimir Levin <vmpstr@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717831}
